<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19054" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fūnĕrārĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>relating to a funeral</i>
			(post-class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">actio,</span>”
				<i>on account of the expenses of a funeral</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Dig. 11, 7, 14, § 6</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">ib. 21 al.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fūnĕrārĭus</span></b> ,
				ii, m., <i>one who took
				charge of funerals</i>, <i>an undertaker</i>,
			Firm. 3, 6 <i>med.</i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
